# Normalise line endings.
#
# The working tree drifted to CRLF (edited from Windows) while every blob in
# the repository is LF, so `git diff` reported ~20,000 changed lines across
# essentially every tracked file. Real changes became impossible to review,
# and a release diff could not be sanity-checked before deploy.
#
# `* text=auto` tells git to store text files with LF in the repository and
# leave the working copy alone. After adding this file, run once:
#
#     git add --renormalize .
#     git commit -m "Normalise line endings to LF"
#
# ...and diffs go back to showing only what actually changed.
* text=auto

# Explicit for the file types in this project, so the heuristic never has to
# guess on an unusual file.
*.php   text eol=lf
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.tsx   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.sql   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.webmanifest text eol=lf
.htaccess     text eol=lf
.env.example  text eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
